    match => { "AGENT_INTERACTION_PATTERN" => "Agent %{INT:agent_id1} interacted with Agent %{INT:agent_id2}: Action=%{WORD:action}, Result=%{WORD:result}(, Duration=%{INT:duration}ms)?" }
  }
}
```

### Conclusion

By using multiple Grok patterns, conditionals, named capture groups, and custom patterns, you can effectively handle log entries with varying formats. This approach ensures that your Logstash configuration is flexible and robust, capable of parsing a wide range of log structures efficiently.

